{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1788472956883869001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"depraved-classless-rooster","assignee":null,"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":4,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"30a3a22b1a18e07b6816bd260cfe1b13bbda162e625d77ace6d3b58e7117a071","event_uuid":"960e49fd-984a-4f49-bfbd-fac38f49afc1","position":{"commit_sha":"866e0c65bdea762307749ae50e51d8a665521fb9","position":"1788469697004204527-960e49fd-984a-4f49-bfbd-fac38f49afc1"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"ccf9ddc9fdb2fde83a2dc439e6969c59f2e057f6acca03630202e29ed5daa282","event_uuid":"bc521c16-64ab-44ac-807b-c49c17f9a2a2","position":{"commit_sha":"36e352a20040e3dbf291e3b0dbeb31311baf6759","position":"1788469880580212317-bc521c16-64ab-44ac-807b-c49c17f9a2a2"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"2c7a1850a8ccaa9078feca7f380d2952f48a79f7e253b7d2711d0417282759be","event_uuid":"a15038d1-3cef-4671-b4b2-9855bae05dad","position":{"commit_sha":"3b789e2c51fd6f59ec24f302df69e00ac020680e","position":"1788469891736198964-a15038d1-3cef-4671-b4b2-9855bae05dad"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"5af8c88c3ca1d576e8926765ab487d80c6ba2e9700a94e2d6196495d5208609b","event_uuid":"04041141-ea90-4318-ba98-9952344c10fb","position":{"commit_sha":"2c0faae1c7cd85ad1f75d0daf7911331557a95c6","position":"1788469909036290266-04041141-ea90-4318-ba98-9952344c10fb"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1788469697004204527,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"bc521c16-64ab-44ac-807b-c49c17f9a2a2","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"afe3-5aec-51cb-4e02"}],"description":"## Context\n\nAfter `forcible-diminished-lamb` and `salmon-abominable-pupa`, both review pipelines have Terraform-scoped tool sessions [rebar:salmon-abominable-pupa]. This slice adds `probe_source` so agents can disprove a claim that a declared module/provider source is unavailable when the source is already local or its registry metadata is positively reachable. It never downloads module content and never treats failed access as nonexistence.\n\n## Scope\n\nAdd `src/rebar/grounding/terraform_source.py` and expose `probe_source(source, from_module)` through the established Terraform-only Pass-1 and Pass-2 sessions.\n\n### Local sources\n\n- Normalize Terraform's literal local source forms relative to `from_module`.\n- Return positive T1 structural evidence only when the resolved directory remains under the repository root, contains an indexable Terraform module, and is included in the bounded immutable closure.\n- An absolute path, an escaping `../`, an escaping symlink, an unreadable directory, a missing target, or a dynamic source returns ABSTAIN. Absence is never asserted.\n- Already-downloaded `.terraform/modules` content is excluded: it is generated, may be stale, and is not part of the client project's attested source snapshot.\n\n### Registry metadata\n\n- Recognize Terraform provider registry addresses and native module registry addresses, including an explicit hostname. Normalize omitted provider/module hostnames to Terraform's documented default.\n- Use Terraform Registry service discovery and version/metadata endpoints only. Accept a source as positive T0 evidence only after a bounded HTTPS response is successful, size-limited, and schema-valid. Do not follow or request any module download URL returned by metadata.\n- Permit the public default registry. For a custom host, permit a globally routable DNS target or an exact hostname trusted by an ambient Terraform credential entry. Reject embedded URL credentials, literal IP targets, non-HTTPS services, and cross-host redirects. A private-address custom host requires the exact credentialed hostname.\n- Bound metadata to 1 MiB per response and the existing 60-second grounding deadline. Use the existing fail-open HTTP seam/harness; no new HTTP dependency.\n- A 2xx schema-valid response yields only count/digest/source-kind facts, never response bodies or remote source contents.\n\n### Ambient credentials\n\nFollow Terraform's precedence and hostname normalization for:\n\n1. `TF_TOKEN_<hostname>` environment credentials.\n2. The static file selected by `TF_CLI_CONFIG_FILE`, else platform-default Terraform CLI config.\n3. Terraform's static `credentials.tfrc.json`.\n\nRead only literal `credentials` entries for the exact registry hostname. Never prompt, write a credential file, execute a `credentials_helper`, import cloud/provider credentials, or use credentials for another host. Output/receipts/logs identify only `auth_source=environment|static-file|none`; they contain no token, token hash, home path, header, or raw error body.\n\n### Error and outcome contract\n\n`probe_source` uses `job=refute`: a positive registry hit returns `refuted` at T0 and a positive local module returns `refuted` at T1, disproving asserted absence. Every other result is ABSTAIN:\n\n- 401/403/404 and private/ambiguous responses → `private_or_internal_suspected`.\n- 429 → `rate_limited`.\n- DNS/TLS/proxy/5xx/redirect rejection → `network_error`.\n- deadline → `timeout`.\n- malformed/oversized metadata → `parse_error`.\n- dynamic, unsupported, or non-registry remote source → `ambiguous`.\n\nNo arm emits an “absent”, “missing”, clean, or negative match.\n\n## Positive rationale\n\nPositive-only metadata mirrors Rebar's existing package-existence oracle and preserves its asymmetric safety: reachable evidence can refute a weak LLM claim, while inaccessible evidence says nothing. Exact-host ambient credentials meet already-authenticated users where they are without adding Rebar auth configuration.\n\n## Out of scope\n\nRemote module downloads/fetch, Git/HTTP/S3/GCS source checkout, Terraform Cloud API operations beyond registry discovery, credential helpers, new auth configuration, provider/cloud credentials, and all Terraform/OpenTofu/provider execution. The ADR must state that ambient-credential remote content fetch is approved as a future feature if demand justifies the additional containment; it is not implemented in V1.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Local-source tests return positive T1 evidence for a literal repo-contained child and ABSTAIN for missing, absolute, escaping, symlink-escaping, unreadable, generated-cache, and dynamic sources without exposing partial facts.\n- [ ] Registry protocol tests return positive T0 evidence only for successful schema-valid provider/module metadata and assert that no download URL or module archive endpoint is requested.\n- [ ] Credential-precedence tests cover Terraform hostname encoding, environment-over-static precedence, `TF_CLI_CONFIG_FILE`, platform defaults, and `credentials.tfrc.json`; helper blocks are ignored and no credential value/hash/path appears in results, receipts, logs, or raised test diagnostics.\n- [ ] The access matrix maps 401/403/404, 429, DNS, TLS, proxy, 5xx, rejected redirect, timeout, malformed JSON, and oversized response to the specified closed abstention and never to nonexistence.\n- [ ] Network-target tests allow the public default registry, a globally routable custom registry, and an exact credentialed private hostname while rejecting HTTP, embedded credentials, literal IPs, uncredentialed private targets, and cross-host redirects before sending a token.\n- [ ] Plan-review T10 and code-review IaC Pass 1/Pass 2 advertise `probe_source` with the two prerequisite operations; non-Terraform steps and missing-extra runs advertise none.\n- [ ] `docs/adr/0111-terraform-structural-grounding.md` and `docs/grounding.md` distinguish V1 metadata probing from prohibited remote fetch and record future ambient-credential fetch as approved-but-deferred.\n\n## Testing\n\nTest contract card:\n\n- Authoritative contract: REB-640, Terraform's registry/CLI-credential protocols, and the prerequisite tool-session contract [rebar:salmon-abominable-pupa].\n- Preconditions: temp repo local modules plus a stateful registry fake serving valid, auth-required, error, redirect, oversized, and download-advertising responses.\n- Production path: real source normalization/credential selection/HTTP response parser through the tool; only DNS/socket transport is faked.\n- Tiers: unit tests for paths/credentials; stateful external-service contract tests for registry mapping; workflow integration for tool visibility.\n- Oracles: exact outcome/tier/reason and requested endpoint/headers, with byte scans proving the secret and download URL never escape or get fetched.\n- Negative controls: a valid public hit refutes absence; the nearest 404 and authenticated access denial both abstain.\n- CI: `make test`.\n\n## Verification\n\n`env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python -m pytest tests/unit/grounding/test_terraform_source.py tests/unit/workflow/test_terraform_plan_review_tools.py tests/unit/workflow/test_terraform_code_review_tools.py`","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/grounding/terraform_source.py","reason":"normalize local sources, registry addresses, ambient credentials, and positive-only metadata probes"},{"path":"src/rebar/grounding/terraform_tools.py","reason":"expose probe_source through the existing Terraform-scoped per-call session"},{"path":"tests/unit/grounding/test_terraform_source.py","reason":"path containment, credential precedence, registry protocol, redaction, and abstention contract"},{"path":"tests/unit/workflow/test_terraform_plan_review_tools.py","reason":"plan-review Pass-1 and Pass-2 probe_source routing"},{"path":"tests/unit/workflow/test_terraform_code_review_tools.py","reason":"code-review IaC Pass-1 and Pass-2 probe_source routing"},{"path":"docs/adr/0111-terraform-structural-grounding.md","reason":"record source trust boundary and approved-but-deferred ambient remote fetch"},{"path":"docs/grounding.md","reason":"document local and registry source probing, credentials, limits, and access-error abstention"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["depends_on","afe3-5aec-51cb-4e02"],["parent","a374-849c-c8f2-4234"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"a374-849c-c8f2-4234","parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["terraform","grounding","registry","credentials","optional"],"ticket_id":"1c52-5e73-4d61-4124","ticket_type":"story","title":"Probe local and registry Terraform sources with ambient access","verify_commands":[{"command":"env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python -m pytest tests/unit/grounding/test_terraform_source.py -k local_source","dd_id":"AC1","dd_text":"repo-contained local hit and every path-containment abstention"},{"command":"env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python -m pytest tests/unit/grounding/test_terraform_source.py -k registry","dd_id":"AC2,AC4,AC5","dd_text":"positive-only registry protocol, target policy, no-download assertion, and access-error matrix"},{"command":"env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python -m pytest tests/unit/grounding/test_terraform_source.py -k credentials","dd_id":"AC3","dd_text":"Terraform credential precedence plus byte-level secret and path redaction"},{"command":"env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python -m pytest tests/unit/workflow/test_terraform_plan_review_tools.py tests/unit/workflow/test_terraform_code_review_tools.py -k probe_source","dd_id":"AC6","dd_text":"Terraform-only Pass-1/Pass-2 visibility and missing-extra negative controls"},{"command":"env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python -m pytest tests/unit/grounding/test_terraform_source.py && env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make docs-check","dd_id":"AC7","dd_text":"source-probe contract and approved-but-deferred remote-fetch documentation"}]},"source_event_uuids":["960e49fd-984a-4f49-bfbd-fac38f49afc1","bc521c16-64ab-44ac-807b-c49c17f9a2a2","a15038d1-3cef-4671-b4b2-9855bae05dad","04041141-ea90-4318-ba98-9952344c10fb"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788472956883869001,"uuid":"6f7be42b-1148-41f5-b9f8-b69d36c72774"}